{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2128 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "0fd77aa90f6a2dff7583ad107798d445593d5dd9ae48433bd4d6edd0843e4836" :edb/db-before-t 2127 :edb/db-after-t 2128 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535440 50 #inst "2026-10-09T00:06:23.643Z" 13194139535440 true] [17592186198373 1020 #edb/ref 17592186349296 13194139535440 true] [17592186198373 1020 #edb/ref 17592186349303 13194139535440 true] [17592186198374 1020 #edb/ref 17592186349306 13194139535440 true] [17592186198374 1020 #edb/ref 17592186349310 13194139535440 true] [17592186198374 1020 #edb/ref 17592186349313 13194139535440 true] [17592186349296 1017 #edb/ref 17592186349297 13194139535440 true] [17592186349296 1089 "q-179539" 13194139535440 true] [17592186349296 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535440 true] [17592186349296 1100 "Given that $P(A)=\\frac{1}{2},$ $P(B)=\\frac{2}{5},$ and $P(A\\cup B)=\\frac{7}{10},$ find $P(A\\cup {B}^{′}).$" 13194139535440 true] [17592186349296 1113 #uuid "5fe77a5c-4312-5b94-9b61-405a56afc897" 13194139535440 true] [17592186349296 1145 "First, we calculate $P(A\\cap B)$ using the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A\\cup B) & =P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B) \\\\ \\frac{7}{10} & =\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{2}{5}-P(A\\cap B) \\\\ P(A\\cap B) & =\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{2}{5}-\\frac{7}{10} \\\\ P(A\\cap B) & =\\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we construct the corresponding Venn diagram and shade the region $A\\cup {B}^{′}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064054/assets/5ecc7dae3e6b6e57ccd4a7b8907cb4dd20b0ece400a5768b747f3cb3da788e4b.png)\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\nP(A\\cup {B}^{′})=\\frac{3}{10}+\\frac{1}{5}+\\frac{3}{10}=\\frac{4}{5}.\n$$" 13194139535440 true] [17592186349297 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349298 13194139535440 true] [17592186349297 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349299 13194139535440 true] [17592186349297 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349300 13194139535440 true] [17592186349297 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349301 13194139535440 true] [17592186349297 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349302 13194139535440 true] [17592186349297 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535440 true] [17592186349297 1041 "selection" 13194139535440 true] [17592186349297 1104 #edb/ref 17592186349299 13194139535440 true] [17592186349297 1110 #uuid "8648fee5-2807-506e-9132-b7540548afdc" 13194139535440 true] [17592186349298 1034 "\\frac{3}{10}" 13194139535440 true] [17592186349298 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535440 true] [17592186349298 1111 #uuid "52c78070-3a7e-52fa-95cb-712b749aa21f" 13194139535440 true] [17592186349299 1034 "\\frac{4}{5}" 13194139535440 true] [17592186349299 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535440 true] [17592186349299 1111 #uuid "a301ec8c-bf6b-5c14-9f67-9a616b6f6135" 13194139535440 true] [17592186349300 1034 "\\frac{2}{5}" 13194139535440 true] [17592186349300 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535440 true] [17592186349300 1111 #uuid "5cfff7ee-5653-54e1-9d64-a27f7e4bfa05" 13194139535440 true] [17592186349301 1034 "\\frac{1}{5}" 13194139535440 true] [17592186349301 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535440 true] [17592186349301 1111 #uuid "93751f4d-3d21-5cc9-bf2a-b1f1a2772bcc" 13194139535440 true] [17592186349302 1034 "\\frac{7}{10}" 13194139535440 true] [17592186349302 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535440 true] [17592186349302 1111 #uuid "6bdf0f46-e510-57fb-9196-c84f08486ee6" 13194139535440 true] [17592186349303 1017 #edb/ref 17592186349304 13194139535440 true] [17592186349303 1089 "q-264403" 13194139535440 true] [17592186349303 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535440 true] [17592186349303 1100 "Given that $P(A)=0.25,$ $P(B)=0.45,$ and $P(A\\cup B)=0.6,$ find $P(A\\cup {B}^{′}).$\n\n$P(A\\cup {B}^{′})=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139535440 true] [17592186349303 1113 #uuid "afce1321-9dc1-5a34-b2c6-72efabe0368c" 13194139535440 true] [17592186349303 1145 "First, we calculate $P(A\\cap B)$ using the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A\\cup B) & =P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B) \\\\ 0.6 & =0.25+0.45-P(A\\cap B) \\\\ P(A\\cap B) & =0.25+0.45-0.6 \\\\  & =0.1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we construct the corresponding Venn diagram and shade the region $A\\cup {B}^{′}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064054/assets/f8fb716593a35fc1f85ab524dc78bf0fa0cd03dc16b0c5ca92a9b2836e6e7c5b.png)\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\nP(A\\cup {B}^{′})=0.15+0.1+0.4=0.65.\n$$" 13194139535440 true] [17592186349304 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349305 13194139535440 true] [17592186349304 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535440 true] [17592186349304 1041 "field-1" 13194139535440 true] [17592186349304 1104 #edb/ref 17592186349305 13194139535440 true] [17592186349304 1110 #uuid "53855a49-5e83-52e8-a0e4-3c60ff6a5cd8" 13194139535440 true] [17592186349305 1034 "0.65" 13194139535440 true] [17592186349305 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535440 true] [17592186349305 1111 #uuid "a088d687-f56b-5771-86ee-ba5215245646" 13194139535440 true] [17592186349306 1017 #edb/ref 17592186349307 13194139535440 true] [17592186349306 1089 "q-264416" 13194139535440 true] [17592186349306 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535440 true] [17592186349306 1100 "Given that $P(B)=0.45,$ $P(A\\cap B)=0.2,$ and $P(A\\cup B)=0.75,$ find $P({A}^{′}).$\n\n$P({A}^{′})=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139535440 true] [17592186349306 1113 #uuid "c1421b79-b763-507f-bc9d-72470c20c64a" 13194139535440 true] [17592186349306 1145 "First, we calculate $P(A)$ using the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A\\cup B) & =P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B) \\\\ 0.75 & =P(A)+0.45-0.2 \\\\ P(A) & =0.75+0.2-0.45 \\\\  & =0.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P({A}^{′}) & =1-P(A) \\\\  & =1-0.5 \\\\  & =0.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535440 true] [17592186349307 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349308 13194139535440 true] [17592186349307 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349309 13194139535440 true] [17592186349307 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535440 true] [17592186349307 1041 "field-1" 13194139535440 true] [17592186349307 1104 #edb/ref 17592186349309 13194139535440 true] [17592186349307 1110 #uuid "e3d64430-ebc6-5724-be8e-77d588adbd85" 13194139535440 true] [17592186349308 1034 "0.25" 13194139535440 true] [17592186349308 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535440 true] [17592186349308 1111 #uuid "346a03b2-edfe-57d2-aece-c0791f822b6e" 13194139535440 true] [17592186349309 1034 "0.5" 13194139535440 true] [17592186349309 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535440 true] [17592186349309 1111 #uuid "43ba118a-6d5e-5035-ae23-fb3680b5ae34" 13194139535440 true] [17592186349310 1017 #edb/ref 17592186349311 13194139535440 true] [17592186349310 1089 "q-264424" 13194139535440 true] [17592186349310 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535440 true] [17592186349310 1100 "Given that $P(B)=\\frac{4}{15},$ $P(A\\cap B)=\\frac{1}{15},$ and $P(A\\cup B)=\\frac{4}{5},$ find $P({A}^{′}).$\n\n$P({A}^{′})=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139535440 true] [17592186349310 1113 #uuid "fea666e2-5052-54f2-889f-1e9563ba7916" 13194139535440 true] [17592186349310 1145 "First, we calculate $P(A)$ using the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A\\cup B) & =P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B) \\\\ \\frac{4}{5} & =P(A)+\\frac{4}{15}-\\frac{1}{15} \\\\ P(A) & =\\frac{4}{5}+\\frac{1}{15}-\\frac{4}{15} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P({A}^{′}) & =1-P(A) \\\\  & =1-\\frac{3}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535440 true] [17592186349311 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349312 13194139535440 true] [17592186349311 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535440 true] [17592186349311 1041 "field-1" 13194139535440 true] [17592186349311 1104 #edb/ref 17592186349312 13194139535440 true] [17592186349311 1110 #uuid "78a12c31-13a3-5cb7-9c7d-1c91bc8cee33" 13194139535440 true] [17592186349312 1034 "\\frac{2}{5}" 13194139535440 true] [17592186349312 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535440 true] [17592186349312 1111 #uuid "8128fbed-1512-5c5c-a0b0-b281928ce934" 13194139535440 true] [17592186349313 1017 #edb/ref 17592186349314 13194139535440 true] [17592186349313 1089 "q-87262" 13194139535440 true] [17592186349313 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535440 true] [17592186349313 1100 "Given that $P(A)=0.5,$ $P(A\\cap B)=0.4,$ and $P(A\\cup B)=0.8,$ find $P({B}^{′}).$" 13194139535440 true] [17592186349313 1113 #uuid "00c1523d-9863-50ec-80df-9eb6aeec0d90" 13194139535440 true] [17592186349313 1145 "First, we calculate $P(B)$ using the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A\\cup B) & =P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B) \\\\ 0.8 & =0.5+P(B)-0.4 \\\\ P(B) & =0.8+0.4-0.5 \\\\ P(B) & =0.7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P({B}^{′}) & =1-P(B) \\\\  & =1-0.7 \\\\  & =0.3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535440 true] [17592186349314 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349315 13194139535440 true] [17592186349314 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349316 13194139535440 true] [17592186349314 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349317 13194139535440 true] [17592186349314 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349318 13194139535440 true] [17592186349314 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349319 13194139535440 true] [17592186349314 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535440 true] [17592186349314 1041 "selection" 13194139535440 true] [17592186349314 1104 #edb/ref 17592186349317 13194139535440 true] [17592186349314 1110 #uuid "ee719a31-a594-548f-a8ff-a20b253ef531" 13194139535440 true] [17592186349315 1034 "0.7" 13194139535440 true] [17592186349315 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535440 true] [17592186349315 1111 #uuid "975c147b-230b-5de4-9147-1fae2e1c2bee" 13194139535440 true] [17592186349316 1034 "0.4" 13194139535440 true] [17592186349316 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535440 true] [17592186349316 1111 #uuid "5c2b88c5-ec29-5fcb-8eac-005baf602a19" 13194139535440 true] [17592186349317 1034 "0.3" 13194139535440 true] [17592186349317 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535440 true] [17592186349317 1111 #uuid "90fb192a-bc92-55ed-bf3c-af4e642a7a61" 13194139535440 true] [17592186349318 1034 "0.8" 13194139535440 true] [17592186349318 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045